<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mostaganem</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mostaganem is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a>. In 1558 the Count of Alcaudete, Spanish governor of Oran, led an army against it and was defeated and killed by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s worst setbacks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Under Ottoman rule it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of the West, and the French occupied it in 1833.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mostaganem.jpg" alt="Mostaganem" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BullyanDZ · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_arsa_gate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
